iterations.reply:
Two notes on choices I had to make:

- **Enrichment query:** `run-info` has no text field, so `<the input's text>` is filled with `info.date`, percent-encoded.
- **Store key:** the contract doesn't name one, so I read the key `urls` from the `subscriptions` store. The value is treated as newline-separated URLs.

The enrichment result is discarded and a failed fetch is ignored, so the output is unchanged. A request outside the host allowlist still traps at the boundary, as the interface specifies.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;
use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

fn encode(s: &str) -> String {
    let mut out = String::new();
    for b in s.bytes() {
        match b {
            b'A'..=b'Z' | b'a'..=b'z' | b'0'..=b'9' | b'-' | b'_' | b'.' | b'~' => {
                out.push(b as char)
            }
            _ => out.push_str(&format!("%{:02X}", b)),
        }
    }
    out
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        // Enrichment fetch; result is intentionally not used, so output is unchanged.
        let url = format!(
            "https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q={}",
            encode(&info.date)
        );
        let _ = http_client::fetch(&url);

        let raw = state_read::get("urls").unwrap_or_default();
        let urls: Vec<String> = raw
            .lines()
            .map(|l| l.trim())
            .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
            .map(|l| l.to_string())
            .collect();

        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

